  "finding": {
    "mechanism": "The old expr_breaks only recognized coalescing and parentheses. A break hidden in a catch handler was absent from contains_break, so a loop that could exit was treated as non-returning and a non-unit function could be accepted without producing a return value.",
    "old_rust_consequence": "Generated value() reaches YV_UNREACHABLE(), defined as __builtin_unreachable() in the runtime, when its catch handler breaks. The undefined behavior follows from the reachable C path; the generated programs were not executed.",
    "old_subset_consequence": "The baseline selfhost subset also accepts the standard-library catch-break reproducer and emits a non-void C function that falls through while main consumes the return value.",
    "runtime_definition": {
      "expansion": "__builtin_unreachable()",
      "line": 42,
      "macro": "YV_UNREACHABLE()",
      "path": "compiler/runtime/yavo_rt.h",
